# Local-only tests: exercise your real machine (your worktrees, your Claude
# sessions, your config) without shipping them. Go compiles them like any
# other test, so they run in `go test ./...` here and are invisible to
# everyone else. Keep them self-contained -- a committed test must never
# depend on a helper defined in one of these files, or you break the build
# for every other clone.
*_local_test.go
